# HooshyarOS Cline execution rules

## Role
Cline is a local VS Code execution/operator layer. It is NOT the architecture owner and must not redefine Architecture Freeze V4, governance, product semantics, or completion rules.

## Source of truth
Always read, in order:
1. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_MASTER_CHARTER.md
2. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_GOVERNANCE_CHARTER.md
3. Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
4. Docs/COMMERCIAL_PRODUCT_COMPLETION_CONTRACT.md
5. Assistant/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md
6. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_CONSTRUCTION_ROADMAP.json

## Mandatory execution loop
Run the real product factory, not a simulated audit:
`READ -> AUDIT -> SELECT -> IMPLEMENT -> TEST -> INTEGRATE -> RUN -> ACCEPT -> REPAIR -> TEST -> ACCEPT -> COMMIT -> PUSH -> REPLAN`

Use `npm run product:factory` as the primary local acceptance command.

## Repair behavior
When the factory returns BLOCKED:
- read the emitted JSON evidence;
- identify the first failing stage and root cause;
- make the smallest coherent repair;
- never weaken/remove a failing test to obtain green;
- never modify Architecture Freeze V4 to bypass a failure;
- rerun the focused verification;
- rerun `npm run product:factory`;
- after acceptance passes, run `npm test -- --runInBand`.

## Product acceptance
A green engine/unit test is not commercial completion. The real Windows journey must pass:
`health -> ready -> session -> tenant -> ingestion -> financial analysis -> dashboard -> restart -> same tenant -> restored dashboard`.

## Git discipline
Before risky changes create a checkpoint/commit when possible. Keep one coherent capability/fix per commit. Do not force-push. Do not push or merge unless the repository policy explicitly permits it.

## Cline boundary
Cline may execute commands, inspect files, apply the smallest implementation repair, and run verification. Cline must not invent a new engine, duplicate business semantics, or claim product completion without application and acceptance evidence.
